Changes in version 3.07

We have made a number of minor improvements and changes to F-PROT since the
release of the previous version.

Most of those changes only affect the speed of the program, or the
detection/disinfection of a handful of viruses, but there were a few
changes to the program functionality:

    The program can now be run from two diskettes, which can be necessary
    when the hard disk MBR is corrupted.  You can now put F-PROT.EXE and
    ENGLISH.TX0 on the first diskette and the three .DEF files (SIGN.DEF,
    SIGN2.DEF and MACRO.DEF) on the second.

    F-PROT can now sacn and disinfect Microsoft Project98 files.

    Improved scanning of self-extracting archives.

The total mumber of viruses and Trojans that are now detected by the
program is now above 45200.

We would also like to remind anyone reading this that the Windows version
of F-PROT is now finally available world-wide.  If you have not yet taken
a look at the trial version of FP-WIN, you might want to do so.
